<p>Iran’s sports minister said the country will not take part in the 2026 FIFA World Cup, hosted by the United States along with Canada and Mexico, citing security concerns for Iranian players in the U.S.. The decision puts one of the world’s biggest sporting events squarely in the path of geopolitics, even as FIFA usually tries to keep national-team competition separate from international disputes. The announcement followed comments from FIFA president Gianni Infantino, who said President Trump told him Iran would be welcome to participate. Iranian officials, however, said participation “is not possible” under the current conditions, with some reporting linking the stance to recent U.S. and Israeli strikes on Iran and a broader regional escalation.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/jc4Tf-ck3mSBq38nUmDyOnpHZJU0C82ihWKd-FCkFUTnlUHfzwkBtsyIVpzQERWGe3pehTJ6xOsGTWjJ3rpF7WADoZnYoQKLBOM2Bj_bfC1VA_oAzakOCW6VKZUm8wItLZ12qIBCaSH92rMks7xjKLhkZvFq6_u61JfYc8wZEm6ZxOIW8Qtbg7PHsbJt5n17vOkBQcqdWvfFfX-t' alt='The Iranian national soccer team before a match against Uzbekistan in March 2025.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>State TV interview detail: The minister made the remarks in an interview on Iranian state television, and coverage pointed to a video of the segment circulating online.</li><li>Mixed messaging from the U.S. side: Infantino relayed Trump’s message that Iran would be welcome, while separate reporting quoted Trump saying he “really don&#x27;t care” whether Iran participates.</li><li>Near-term fixtures: NPR reported Iran is set to play three games in the U.S. in June, and observers read the minister’s comments in that context.</li><li>Escalation specifics in some accounts: SCMP linked the boycott signal to U.S.-Israeli strikes and reported Iranian officials referenced the killing of Ayatollah Ali Khamenei when explaining why participation could not go ahead.</li><li>Tournament uncertainty: Deutsche Welle noted that even the possibility of a qualified team stepping away would further politicize planning and make the 2026 field feel less settled.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Iranian Sports and Youth Ministry: Minister Ahmad Donyamali said participation in a U.S.-hosted World Cup is “not possible,” citing safety concerns and, in some reporting, linking the stance directly to the U.S.-Israel strikes and the killing of Iran’s supreme leader. (<a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/03/11/taking-part-in-world-cup-not-possible-says-iranian-sports-minister'>Euronews</a>, <a href='https://www.scmp.com/sport/football/article/3346272/iran-cannot-take-part-united-states-hosted-2026-world-cup-sports-minister-says'>SCMP</a>)</li><li>FIFA leadership: FIFA president Gianni Infantino said President Trump told him Iran would be welcome at the World Cup. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/11/world/europe/trump-iran-world-cup-fifa-infantino.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>U.S. President Donald Trump: The Hindu reported Trump said, “I really don&#x27;t care” whether Iran takes part in the 48-nation tournament. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/sport/football/iran-says-country-cant-take-part-in-fifa-world-cup-2026-because-of-us-attacks/article70732803.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/sport/football/iran-says-country-cant-take-part-in-fifa-world-cup-2026-because-of-us-attacks/article70732803.ece'>Iran says country can&#x27;t take part in FIFA World Cup 2026 because of U.S. attacks</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/11/world/europe/trump-iran-world-cup-fifa-infantino.html'>Iran to Skip World Cup, Minister Says, Despite Reported Trump Assurances to FIFA</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/sport/football/article/3346272/iran-cannot-take-part-united-states-hosted-2026-world-cup-sports-minister-says'>Iran will not compete in United States-hosted 2026 World Cup, sports minister says</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/03/11/nx-s1-5744855/fifa-world-cup-iran-team'>Iran&#x27;s soccer team cannot participate in the FIFA World Cup, Iranian minister says</a> - npr.org</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/irans-sports-minister-says-country-cant-take-part-in-world-cup-because-of-u-s-attacks'>Iran&#x27;s sports minister says country can&#x27;t take part in World Cup because of U.S. attacks</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/03/11/taking-part-in-world-cup-not-possible-says-iranian-sports-minister'>Taking part in World Cup &#x27;not possible&#x27;, says Iranian sports minister</a> - euronews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/iran-signals-2026-world-cup-boycott-after-us-strikes/a-76309956'>Iran signals 2026 World Cup boycott after US strikes</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.reuters.com/sports/soccer/iran-cannot-participate-world-cup-sports-minister-says-2026-03-11/'>Iranian sports minister Ahmad Donyamali states that Iran will not participate in the 2026 FIFA World Cup to be hosted by Canada, Mexico, and the United States, citing security concerns amid the Iran war.</a> - reuters.com</li></ul>